  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="FR">Output 4.1. Increased capacity of Member States to create an enabling environment for entrepreneurship and sustainable enterprises</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="FR">1. EFP trained 80 women in Get Ahead to start their businesses in Sindh and Punjab in 2022. Some of these were linked to e-commerce options, creating opportunities to access more buyers but also creating jobs for others
2. The Women&apos;s Chamber of Commerce promoted safe workplaces through its members. The organization has empowered women entrepreneurs to prioritize the well-being of their workforce while also enhancing business productivity. By championing the cause of safe workspaces, the Women&apos;s Chamber of Commerce has not only bolstered the success of businesses but has also contributed to the overall economic and social development of the community.
 Supported by the Government of Japan, the ILO leveraged the flagship module Get Ahead for vulnerable women in Punjab and Sindh. The module was tailored to the specific needs of this group. The ILO with the government of Japan&apos;s support also leveraged the support of the Employers Federation of Pakistan in delivering capacity building and enabling market linkages
The ILO with funding from Japan also assisted the Women&apos;s Chamber of Commerce in using ILO Convention 190 for the benefit of its members. The ILO provided training on C190 and a forum for knowledge sharing.</narrative>
   </description>
