  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="FR">Output 4.2. Strengthened capacity of enterprises and their support systems to enhance productivity and sustainability</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="FR">&#x2022; Eight enterprises completed a six-month SCORE implementation, resulting in reduction in overall defect rates in the production lines, reduced energy bills, improved productivity, better quality of production, and improved labour retention rates, which have ultimately resulted in significant financial benefits to the businesses.
&#x2022; Thirteen additional textile and leather enterprises are implementing SCORE Lean Programme
&#x2022; Twenty-six local trainers are trained on SCORE Lean programme to provide support to enterprises in two provinces.
&#x2022; Twenty-five medium to large enterprises in the textile and leather sectors are selected for 12-month sustainable capacity development support and implementation has started from August 2023.
&#x2022; Forty textile enterprises&#x2019; units have been supported through a range of interventions to improve their quality, productivity, and working conditions through the ILO&#x2019;s tool on &#x201c;Work Improvements in Small Enterprises (WISE)
&#x2022; Zig Zag methodology benefits 600 Brick kiln owners; with a reach out to 48000 workers on ensuring decent working conditions (with a focus on OSH), productivity, and greening

 &#x2022; With the support of the EU, the ILO trained local trainers to provide help to the enterprises for SCORE implementation 
&#x2022; ILO collaborated with the Kaizen Institute to provide support services to enterprises for sustainable capacity development 
 &#x2022; ILO provided OSH training to small to medium enterprises  
&#x2022; With support from the Government of Italy, training was piloted in Zig Zag and an exposure visit of the BK owners to Italy and exchange of best practices through ILO partners ISCOS was conducted.</narrative>
   </description>
